;MOLECULE DESIGNATED AS CHAIN B BELOW IS PREFERRED FOR
STRUCTURAL COMPARISONS BECAUSE IT IS MORE COMPLETE AND LESS
PERTURBED BY INTERMOLECULAR CONTACTS.

ALTERNATE LOCATIONS *A* AND *B* ARE PARTIALLY OCCUPIED
CONFORMATIONS FOR RESIDUES SER A 64, SER A 150,
HIS B 45, SER B 64 AND ASP B 122.  IN ALL CASES, *A* IS
BELIEVED TO BE THE MAJOR CONFORMER.  NEITHER THE
OCCUPANCIES NOR THE THERMAL PARAMETERS SHOULD BE
CONSIDERED AS RELIABLE.
